h reference in both live consumers named in this item's starting points: `agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` Output Format section and `skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` (both prompt templates), changing `(see .claude/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md)` \u2192 `load dh:dh-meta-docs and read the Backlog Item Groomed Schema document it lists`. Confirmed via `git show 20c84f3b5 -- <path>` on both files. These two consumers do **not** need a path fix as part of #3332 \u2014 only verify the new \\\"load dh-meta-docs\\\" instruction still resolves once #3332's doc fixes land (it should \u2014 dh-meta-docs indexes `docs/*.md` dynamically, see below).\\n- It **deletes** `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/` entirely, including the older, competing schema doc `skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md` and `skills/backlog/templates/item.md` \u2014 both of which used `name:` as the frontmatter title field (the same drift class flagged in this item). Their replacement, `plugins/development-harness/templates/backlog-item.md` (new location, confirmed present on `origin/main`), **still uses `name: ITEM TITLE HERE`** \u2014 so the `name`/`title` field-name drift is not fully resolved upstream either; it has moved, not disappeared. Not fixing `templates/backlog-item.md` is in scope for #3332 only if the item's mandate is read broadly as \\\"make the doc match the model\\\"; recommend flagging it as a related-but-separate follow-up rather than silently expanding this item's diff, since the orchestrator's mandate was specifically `docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`.\\n- `docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` itself (the actual target file) is **untouched** by #3330 \u2014 confirmed via `git show 20c84f3b5 -- plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` (empty diff). The core grooming task remains valid and necessary.\\n\\nNet effect: the real remaining consumer-side work for #3332 is smaller than the starting points implied \u2014 two of three named \\\"broken path\\\" sites are already fixed upstream, and the domain-registry.md file is already deleted upstream. The task should verify against `origin/main` state, not this worktree's `main`, when planning.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `backlog_core/models.py::BacklogItem` (~L1011-1013) \u2014 canonical field is `title: str = \\\"\\\"`. No `name` field exists on `BacklogItem` or `BacklogItemMetadata` (~L760-796). The doc's frontmatter example (`name: \\\"Item title\\\"`) does not match this model.\\n- `backlog_core/models.py::_VALID_STATUSES` (L723) \u2014 canonical set `{\\\"open\\\", \\\"done\\\", \\\"in-progress\\\", \\\"needs-grooming\\\", \\\"closed\\\"}`. The doc's frontmatter example (`status: open|in-progress|done|resolved`) includes a legacy-only value (`resolved`, explicitly documented at `_validate_status` L882-896 as \\\"preserved as-is\\\" but not canonical) and omits two canonical values (`needs-grooming`, `closed`).\\n- `backlog_core/yaml_io.py::save_item()` (L84-132) \u2014 serializes `item.model_dump(exclude={\\\"file_path\\\",\\\"skip\\\"})`, which emits the model's `title` field, never `name`. Any item groomed/saved today round-trips as `title:`, contradicting the doc's `name:` example.\\n- `backlog_core/parsing.py` (L363, L1368) \u2014 `title=str(fm.get(\\\"name\\\") or fm.get(\\\"title\\\") or \\\"\\\")` \u2014 `name` is accepted only as a **legacy read-time alias** for backward compatibility with old files, never written back. The doc should describe this as a legacy-input alias, not present `name` as the current field.\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 groom write path (`_write_groomed_to_item` L1042, `_write_groomed_to_reference` L1103, `_apply_groomed_update` L3523, `_handle_update_groomed` L1183) \u2014 the functions that actually persist `## Groomed` content per the schema this doc defines.\\n- `backlog_core/backends/` \u2014 four backend implementations of the work-item protocol: `GitHubBackend` (github_backend.py, uses `github_work_items.py` which is the only backend touching `yaml_io`/per-item `.yaml` files as a local cache), `SQLiteBackend` (sqlite_backend.py), `InMemoryBackend` (memory_backend.py), `BeadsBackend` (beads_backend.py). Only the GitHub backend's local cache uses the per-item-file layout the doc's \\\"Location\\\" section describes; SQLite, memory, and beads backends store items without that file path existing at all. The doc's **\\\"Location\\\" framing is backend-specific to one of four backends**, confirming the orchestrator's starting-point concern.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` (Output Format section, ~L427-429) \u2014 **on this worktree's `main`**, still hardcodes the broken `.claude/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` path. **Already fixed on `origin/main` by #3330** (routes through `dh:dh-meta-docs` instead). No action needed here if the branch this item lands on is rebased past #3330; otherwise this file still needs the same fix independently.\\n- `skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` (dispatch prompt templates, ~L33, L74) \u2014 same broken-path pattern, same status: already fixed on `origin/main` by #3330.\\n- `skills/backlog-tools-administrator/references/domain-registry.md:72` \u2014 cites the same broken `.claude/docs/...` path. Already **deleted entirely** on `origin/main` by #3330 (whole skill removed as dead). No fix needed if working from current upstream state \u2014 this file plus its `.claude/skills/` mirror copy will not exist.\\n- `docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` (L314, L357) \u2014 cites this doc as a cross-check source for the `Backlog Item Sections` provenance table. Citation is by path only (`docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md (L64\u201381)`), not by field content, so it is not affected by the `name`/`status` drift directly, but should be re-verified after this item's edits if line numbers L64-81 shift.\\n- `skills/dh-meta-docs/SKILL.md` \u2014 **verified, not speculative**: this skill does not hardcode a list of docs. It dynamically indexes every file via `` !`find ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs -name '*.md' -type f | sort` `` and instructs the reading agent to \\\"Read any file above to learn about that topic.\\\" Because `docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` lives under `plugins/development-harness/docs/`, it is **already** picked up by this glob today \u2014 it does not need to be added as a \\\"third consumer\\\"; it already is one, indirectly, via dynamic discovery rather than a hardcoded reference. This is the mechanism #3330 relies on when it redirects `backlog-item-groomer.md` and `groomer-agent.md` to \\\"load dh:dh-meta-docs and read the schema document it lists\\\" instead of hardcoding the path.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md` (frontmatter `sources:` list, L16, L55, L1103) \u2014 a dated (2026-05-14) point-in-time research snapshot comparing GitHub-backend vs. a proposed beads backend. Cites this doc as a source. Not a live instruction consumer \u2014 informational/historical, no update required, but flagged for completeness.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` \u2014 the file to be fixed (frontmatter `name:` \u2192 `title:`; \\\"Location\\\" section rewritten to acknowledge multi-backend reality instead of a single hardcoded per-item-file path; status vocabulary example aligned to `_VALID_STATUSES`).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/templates/backlog-item.md` (new location post-#3330, replaces deleted `skills/backlog/templates/item.md`) \u2014 still uses `name: ITEM TITLE HERE` in its frontmatter template, the same field-name drift. Related but out of this item's named scope (item creation template, not the groomed-content schema doc); recommend a follow-up item rather than silent scope creep here.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\nNone identified. No `.yml`/`.yaml` CI workflow or config file references `backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` (grepped `.github` and all `*.yml`/`*.yaml` repo-wide \u2014 zero hits).\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` \u2014 see Code \u2014 Consumers above (already fixed on `origin/main`, verify state before planning a duplicate task).\\n- `skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` \u2014 see Code \u2014 Consumers above (same).\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `backlog_core/models.py` \u2014 Pydantic schema, source of truth for field names/status vocabulary.\\n- `backlog_core/parsing.py` \u2014 legacy-format ingestion (accepts `name` as read-only alias).\\n- `backlog_core/yaml_io.py` \u2014 canonical write path for `.yaml` item files (GitHub-backend local cache only).\\n- `backlog_core/rendering.py` + `backlog_core/section_registry.py` \u2014 `SECTION_HEADING` registry governing which `## Groomed` subsections round-trip; already cross-checked against this doc by `KNOWN_ENTITIES.md`'s 2026-08-18 (#2979) reconciliation pass \u2014 no drift found there, out of scope for #3332.\\n- `backlog_core/backends/{github_backend,sqlite_backend,memory_backend,beads_backend}.py` \u2014 four backend implementations; only one uses the file-path layout this doc describes.\\n- `agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`, `skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` \u2014 the two live prompt-template consumers.\\n- `skills/dh-meta-docs/SKILL.md` \u2014 dynamic doc index; the intended discovery path post-#3330.\\n- `docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` \u2014 cross-check/provenance ledger citing this doc by path and line range.\\n- `templates/backlog-item.md` \u2014 sibling doc with the same `name`/`title` drift, out of named scope but related.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [x] Every code producer identified (models.py, parsing.py, yaml_io.py, operations.py, 4 backend implementations)\\n- [x] Every code consumer identified, and current state (this worktree vs. `origin/main`) reconciled for each\\n- [x] Every stale document identified (target doc itself, plus related `templates/backlog-item.md`)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated \u2014 none identified, N/A\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed \u2014 N/A, this is a doc-accuracy fix, not an interface change\\n- [x] Agent instructions checked \u2014 both named consumers already fixed on `origin/main`; verify branch base before creating duplicate tasks\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:51:41.025305Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Pre-implementation sync consideration (not in-scope work for this item):** this worktree's local `main` is 1 commit behind `origin/main`. That commit (#3330) already fixed the two live consumers' hardcoded doc-path references (`agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`, `skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md`), redirecting both to dynamic `dh:dh-meta-docs` discovery instead of a hardcoded path. Before planning/implementing this item, verify against `origin/main` state (rebase past #3330, or diff-check) so this item's diff doesn't duplicate or conflict with already-landed consumer-side fixes. The item's own target file (`docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`) is confirmed untouched by #3330, so the core fix remains valid regardless.\\n- No blocking dependencies on other open or in-flight backlog items. RT-ICA verdict is READY with zero MISSING conditions.\\n- Related-but-separate: `templates/backlog-item.md` has the same `name`/`title` field drift; flagged by Impact Radius as a follow-up candidate, explicitly out of this item's named scope.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:51:41.025083Z</sub>\\n\\nP1 (confirmed). This is not a cosmetic doc-polish issue \u2014 the file is an active dispatch-time reference for AI agents performing backlog grooming, and is read today via `dh:dh-meta-docs`'s dynamic index of `docs/*.md` regardless of hardcoded path references. An agent following the doc as written would emit a nonexistent `name:` frontmatter field, describe storage as `.md` file-path-based (wrong for 3 of 4 backends and wrong extension for the 4th), and offer an invalid status vocabulary \u2014 all of which would need to be caught and corrected downstream rather than being correct at the source.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:51:41.025153Z</sub>\\n\\n- Groomed backlog content produced by agents following this doc will use the actual `BacklogItem` schema (`title`/`reference`/`description`) instead of a nonexistent `name:` field.\\n- Status values agents write will be drawn from the real canonical set (`_VALID_STATUSES`), eliminating invalid values (`resolved`) and omissions (`needs-grooming`, `closed`).\\n- The schema description becomes backend-agnostic, correctly describing content that flows through `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)` regardless of which of the four backends (github/sqlite/memory/beads) is configured, instead of asserting a GitHub-backend-only file-path layout as if it were universal.\\n- Closes a confirmed instance of undetected doc/code drift, consistent with the item's root-cause finding that no PR-time documentation-sync gate currently exists for this file.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:44:52.771672Z</sub>\\n\\n**MISSION_ALIGNED**\\n\\nThis documentation-accuracy fix directly enforces the development-harness's core design principle that agents work exclusively with logical models and backend-agnostic schemas, not physical storage details or provider-specific framing.\\n\\n**Mission alignment citations:**\\n\\n- *Logical vs. Physical Boundary* \u2014 AGENTS.md \u00a7State Management: \\\"Agents address plans and tasks logically (`P{id}/T{M}`) through `sam_plan`, `sam_task`, or the grouped DH CLI adapter. **Physical paths, cache records, provider IDs, and wire formats are backend internals.**\\\" The proposed change removes backend-specific \\\"Location\\\" framing that only applies to GitHub backend's file-path structure, stopping 3 of 4 backends (sqlite, memory, beads) from being misled about non-existent file paths.\\n\\n- *Consumer Documentation Boundary* \u2014 PURPOSE.md \u00a7Documentation Frames: \\\"**Consumer documentation must not require contributor documentation for ordinary installation, configuration, usage, or recovery.**\\\" The current doc misleads AI agents (the primary consumer) with inaccurate field names (`name` vs canonical `title`) and incomplete status vocabulary. Correcting these enforces the stated consumer-documentation contract.\\n\\n- *Agent-Facing Workflow Integrity* \u2014 PURPOSE.md \u00a7Purpose: \\\"The plugin is primarily an **agent-facing workflow system expressed in Markdown.**\\\" The backlog-item-groomed-schema doc is read by backlog-item-groomer and other agents as a reference schema. Inaccurate documentation is a direct failure of this promise. Correcting field-name drift against `backlog_core/models.py::BacklogItem` and status vocabulary against `_VALID_STATUSES` restores schema integrity.\\n\\n- *Multi-Backend Abstraction* \u2014 AGENTS.md \u00a7Plugin Identity: \\\"The harness owns the *process*; language plugins own the *specialists*.\\\" The schema doc should express backend-agnostic frontmatter and section structure, not embed assumptions about a single backend's file layout. Removing \\\"Location\\\" framing supports true multi-backend composability.\\n\\n**Scope alignment**: This is a documentation accuracy fix, not an interface change or scope expansion. It corrects documented schema against the authoritative Pydantic model (`title` is the only canonical field; `name` is a legacy read-only alias) and aligns status vocabulary to the canonical set (`_VALID_STATUSES`, currently missing `needs-grooming` and `closed`). The fix preserves all existing grooming behavior while stopping misguidance of AI agents about physical storage details.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:51:41.025217Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`'s frontmatter example no longer shows a `name:` field as a documented/current schema element.\\n- [ ] The doc's frontmatter example matches `BacklogItem`'s real fields per `backlog_core/models.py:1011-1013`.\\n- [ ] The \\\"Location\\\"/storage section no longer presents a single hardcoded per-item file path as the universal storage mechanism across all backends.\\n- [ ] The \\\"Location\\\"/storage section's description holds true for all four backends (github, sqlite, memory, beads), or explicitly scopes any backend-specific detail as backend-specific rather than general.\\n- [ ] The doc's status vocabulary example exactly matches `_VALID_STATUSES` in `backlog_core/models.py:723` (`open`, `done`, `in-progress`, `needs-grooming`, `closed`) with no non-canonical values present.\\n- [ ] No other file changes are introduced \u2014 this item's scope is limited to `docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T11:10:14.045422Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Line ~46's prose rule (\\\"Do not duplicate `name`, `description`, `source`...\\\") no longer references `name` as a current/duplicable field \u2014 corrected to reference the real field (`title`). (Discovered by feature-researcher C1: `name` drift appears twice in the file, not just at line 15.)\\n- [ ] The doc's priority vocabulary example (`:21`, `P0|P1|P2|Ideas`) matches `_VALID_PRIORITIES` in `backlog_core/models.py:721` (`P0`, `P1`, `P2`, `Ideas`, `completed`), with no missing canonical value. (Discovered by feature-researcher C4: same drift class as the already-named status-vocabulary defect, one line away, verified against models.py:721.)\\n- [ ] The broken relative link at `:11` (`[research/README.md](../../research/README.md)`, which resolves to a nonexistent `plugins/research/README.md`) is corrected to resolve to the real `research/README.md` at repo root. (Discovered by feature-researcher C5, verified both paths.)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:51:41.025187Z</sub>\\n\\nAfter the fix, `docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` states:\\n- A frontmatter field list matching `BacklogItem`'s real fields (`title`, `reference`, `description`, per `models.py:1011-1013`), with no `name:` field presented as current schema.\\n- A \\\"Location\\\"/storage description that is backend-agnostic: it describes the frontmatter shape, body sections, and Groomed subsections as content passed through `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)` independent of backend, rather than asserting a single hardcoded per-item `.md` file path that only ever applied to the GitHub backend's local cache (and even there, actual storage is `.yaml`, per `yaml_io.py:87`).\\n- A status vocabulary example matching `_VALID_STATUSES` (`open`, `done`, `in-progress`, `needs-grooming`, `closed`), with the non-canonical `resolved` value removed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:51:41.025333Z</sub>\\n\\nSmall (XS). Single-file documentation edit, three discrete and independently verifiable corrections, no code/interface/behavioral changes, no test suite impact. Primary effort is verifying the worktree-vs-origin/main sync state noted under Dependencies before editing, not the edit itself.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:51:41.025022Z</sub>\\n\\nDeterministic, not intermittent \u2014 this is a static content-drift defect, reproducible 100% of the time simply by reading the file.\\n\\n1. Open `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`.\\n2. Compare line ~15's frontmatter example against `backlog_core/models.py:1011-1013` (`BacklogItem` fields) \u2014 the doc shows a `name:` field that does not exist on the model.\\n3. Compare line ~5's \\\"Location\\\" framing against `backlog_core/yaml_io.py:87` (storage always writes `.yaml`, not `.md`) and against `AGENTS.md`'s Backend Providers section (sqlite/memory/beads backends have no comparable file-path structure at all).\\n4. Compare line ~23's status vocabulary example against `backlog_core/models.py:723`'s `_VALID_STATUSES` \u2014 the doc lists `open|in-progress|done|resolved`, which both omits canonical values (`needs-grooming`, `closed`) and includes a non-canonical one (`resolved`).\\n\\nAll four comparisons fail identically on every read; there is no environment, timing, or backend-selection condition under which the doc's stated schema matches the model.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Follow-up from #3329 (dh:backlog dead-skill cleanup)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Concerns\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T11:38:24.990216Z</sub>\\n\\n- [x] \\\"Example Groomed Body\\\" section (~lines 170, 209) still contains illustrative `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/...` paths \u2014 explicitly out of scope for #3332 (not one of the six edit sites), left untouched deliberately. (reported by dh:task-worker on T1) \u2014 Verified real; filed as follow-up #3342.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T11:49:36.689139Z</sub>\\n\\n- [x] RESOLVED \u2014 T2's AC #6 gap (commit 5921eec17 touched 3 plugin.json manifests alongside the target doc) was caused by this worktree being 2 commits behind origin/main (missing #3330, which deleted skills/backlog-tools-administrator/ and skills/backlog/, and #3337). The auto-sync-manifests pre-commit hook computed its version bump from a stale local baseline. Root-cause fix applied: `git fetch origin main` + `git rebase origin/main` (worktree was clean, single local commit, target doc file confirmed untouched by both upstream commits \u2014 no content conflicts, only the 3 manifest version fields conflicted). Resolved by keeping origin/main's already-correct versions (11.0.0/10.0.0/7.0.0, from #3330's real component deletions) and letting the hook's patch bump apply cleanly on rebase (\u2192 11.0.1/10.0.1/7.0.1). Post-rebase: worktree is 0 behind origin/main, `git diff --stat origin/main HEAD` shows exactly 4 files (the target doc + 3 manifests with a correct patch-level bump each), and the doc content is byte-identical to the pre-rebase version. AC #6's intent (no unrequested file edits by the implementing agent) is satisfied \u2014 the manifest changes are deterministic repo automation, not agent-introduced scope creep.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:37:56.730272Z</sub>\\n\\n**Method**: 5-whys\\n**Classification**: defect\\n\\n#### Evidence Chain\\n\\n1. CLAIM: BacklogItem model has never documented a `name:` field; real fields are `title`, `reference`, `description`\\n   EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 git show 0f3c0fb9b (2026-03-18) BacklogItem first definition shows title/description, not name\\n   VERIFIED: yes\\n   DEPENDS ON: none (symptom)\\n\\n2. CLAIM: Storage format is always `.yaml` regardless of original extension, not `.md` as documented\\n   EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 yaml_io.py:84-87 docstring states \\\"Always writes `.yaml` format regardless of the original file extension\\\"\\n   VERIFIED: yes\\n   DEPENDS ON: 1\\n\\n3. CLAIM: Multi-backend support (sqlite/memory/beads) was implemented in 2026-03-30, making file-path storage framing backend-specific and misleading\\n   EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 git log commit a2b56597a \\\"feat(backlog-core): implement pluggable BacklogBackend protocol\\\"\\n   VERIFIED: yes\\n   DEPENDS ON: 2\\n\\n4. CLAIM: Valid status vocabulary is {open, done, in-progress, needs-grooming, closed}, not the documented {open, in-progress, done, resolved}\\n   EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 models.py:723 `_VALID_STATUSES = {\\\"open\\\", \\\"done\\\", \\\"in-progress\\\", \\\"needs-grooming\\\", \\\"closed\\\"}`\\n   VERIFIED: yes\\n   DEPENDS ON: 1\\n\\n5. CLAIM: Documentation has not been updated since BacklogItem model, storage layer, and backend architecture changed\\n   EVIDENCE: Bash \u2014 git log shows no recent updates to docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md; git log models.py shows multiple changes in last 5 months\\n   VERIFIED: yes\\n   DEPENDS ON: 1, 2, 3, 4\\n\\n**Root Cause**: No documentation-sync review gate exists in the PR merge process. Code changes to BacklogItem, storage formats, and backend architecture proceed without requiring updates to docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md. No CI check validates documentation accuracy against current implementation. Code reviewers do not cross-check doc accuracy as part of merge gates.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0071f000105ea48945234243e159c139024c4bd028baa09afadde8f969002f0a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRfOAlw\"}"}